<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wear</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wear &lt;item&gt; [&lt;location&gt;]
wear all
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>wear helmet
wear ring finger
wear all
</pre>
<p>If you have an item and wish to wear it, you use this command. If you leave out 
the location, the item is fitted in the most natural position it can be worn 
on. <a cmd='#'>wear all</a> puts on everything you carry that you can wear.
</p><p>The locations are: finger, neck, body, head, legs, feet, hands, arms, about, 
waist, wrist, shield, chest, back, ear and ankle. Where there are two (fingers, 
ears), the free one is used.
</p><p>Clothes and armour are made for a size: an item may be too big or too small to 
fit you, and the game tells you so (see <a cmd='#'>Help Resize</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Equipment</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wield</a>
